# Guards on a loop counter, read per trip: the barrier's `k >= 3`
# compares the counter alone, though the loop also holds a branch on
# the thread index; the store's mask compares it with the lanes. Per
# CTA each trip counts its own threads: 6 trips of 64 barriers, and
# 4 trips of 64 stores and one of 44. The loop footprint requests the
# 1200 B the totals store, trip by trip; its distinct and sector bytes
# count every thread the mask admits at some trip on every trip
# (PLAN.md).
RUN: %ptxroof analyze --annotate %fixtures/micro/counter_guard.ptx --bind 1:n=300 | FileCheck --check-prefix=ANN "%s"
RUN: %ptxroof analyze %fixtures/micro/counter_guard.ptx --bind 1:n=300 | FileCheck "%s"
ANN: {{^}}.visible .entry micro_counter_guard( // block 64×1×1 | param_1 = 300 | per CTA: global store 1,200 B; param load 768 B{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}$L__BB0_1: // loop: trips 8 | global per CTA: requested 1,200 B, unique <= 256 B, sectors <= 2,048–2,560 B | warp * × lane * | exec 512/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	bar.sync 	0; // [<block 2>] warp * × lane * | exec 384/CTA{{$}}
ANN: {{^}}	st.global.u32 	[%rd3], %r5; // [<block 4>] <= warp * × lane * | exec 300/CTA | global store [4·%tid.x + param_0] sectors/req <= 5 (ideal 4){{$}}
CHECK: <block 2>  (no line info)       1  <= 64 in <= 2 warps (k[$L__BB0_1] >= 3)
CHECK: <block 4>  (no line info)       1  <= 64 in <= 2 warps (%tid.x + 64 * k[$L__BB0_1] < 364)
CHECK: totals per CTA [static]:
CHECK: bar.sync{{ +}}384{{ +}}12{{$}}
CHECK: st.global.u32{{ +}}300{{ +}}10{{$}}
